# simplecore bundle manifest
#
# One record per vendored file:
#   <source path under .simplecore/>  <destination path in the plugin>  <mode>
#
# mode = copy      byte-identical in every plugin
# mode = template  @PLUGIN@ is rewritten to the host plugin's name
#
# A `SKIP <plugin> <source path>` line excludes one file from one plugin, for
# the cases where the shared version would be a downgrade.  Vendoring a file a
# plugin does not source would leave it to rot unnoticed.
#
# Bump VERSION whenever any source file changes.  vendor.sh stamps the version
# into each plugin's .simplecore.manifest, and `make core-verify` fails the
# build when a plugin's copy no longer matches what the manifest recorded.
VERSION 1

core.vim              autoload/@PLUGIN@/core.vim  copy
install-common.sh     install-common.sh           copy
tests/vim_core.vim    tests/vim_core.vim          template
tests/defcompile.vim  tests/defcompile.vim        copy
tests/fake_daemon.py  tests/fake_daemon.py        copy

# simpleclipboard installs two artifacts (the daemon and a cdylib Vim loads
# with libcall) and stages the whole lib directory with a backup it can roll
# back to.  The shared installer handles one binary and no rollback, so it
# keeps its own.
SKIP simpleclipboard install-common.sh
